sentences.l:
So then having spoken, he led the way from the council, to go,
and they rose up and obeyed the shepherd of the people,
the sceptre-bearing kings;

As the tribes go of bees, thronging,
from a hollow rock ever newly coming forth,
and in clusters they fly over the flowers of spring;

So of them the many tribes, from the ships and the huts,
in front of the deep shore were marching
in troops to the assembly;

So, I suppose, to Zeus exceeding-strong it is likely to be dear,
who indeed of many cities has undone the heads
and still will undo;

And as when the West Wind stirs a deep cornfield, coming
fierce, swooping on it, and it bows down with its ears of grain,
so of them the whole assembly was stirred;

and they with a shout
toward the ships rushed, and from beneath their feet the dust
stood up, rising;

and they were urging one another
to lay hold of the ships and to drag them to the heavenly brine,
and they cleared out the channels;

and they would leave behind a boast for Priam and the Trojans,
Argive Helen, for whose sake many of the Achaeans
in Troy perished, away from their dear fatherland;

